IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-s2-definitions`
IMPORT `sgta-part8-penalties`
IMPORT `sgta-part9-general`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 6 (offences and penalties): ss 53 to 59 and s 64.
-- (ss 60 to 63, 65 to 70: deferred, see COVERAGE.md.  s 71: sgta-s11-approval.l4.)
-- These rules say what each offence section says.  They do not say whether any particular person is caught:
-- a rule takes the facts as inputs and the caller supplies them.
--
-- The 2000 Revised Edition numbers of ss 53, 54, 55 were 33, 34 and 35 (the margin markers in the deposit);
-- the instruments made before the 2020 Revised Edition cite those numbers.

§ `s 53 Unlawful operation of telecommunication system or service`

-- src:4831 | 53.—(1) Subject to this section and section 4, any person who
-- src:4832 | establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates a
-- src:4833 | telecommunication system or service within Singapore without a
-- src:4834 | licence granted under section 5, or during the suspension of the
-- src:4835 | person’s licence under section 10 or otherwise infringes the privilege
-- src:4836 | conferred upon the Authority by section 3 shall be guilty of an
-- src:4837 | offence.
@ref s 53(1) (src:4831-4837)
GIVEN `act` IS AN `Act on a telecommunication system or service`
      `the act is done within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a licence granted under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is suspended under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act otherwise infringes the privilege conferred on the Authority by section 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        (NOT `section 4 applies`)
    AND (   (    (   `act` EQUALS `establishing`
                  OR `act` EQUALS `installing`
                  OR `act` EQUALS `maintaining`
                  OR `act` EQUALS `providing`
                  OR `act` EQUALS `operating`)
             AND `the act is done within Singapore`
             AND (   (NOT `the person holds a licence granted under section 5`)
                  OR `the licence is suspended under section 10`))
         OR `the act otherwise infringes the privilege conferred on the Authority by section 3`)

-- src:4844 | (2) Any person guilty of an offence under this section shall be liable
-- src:4845 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment
-- src:4846 | for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both and, in the case of a
-- src:4847 | continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every
-- src:4848 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:4849 | conviction.
@ref s 53(2) (src:4844-4849)
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`s 53(2): the penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 100000, 36, 10000, FALSE

-- src:4864 | (5) Where the commission by any person of an offence under this
-- src:4865 | section is due to the act or default of some other person, that other
-- src:4866 | person shall be guilty of the offence; and a person may be charged
-- src:4867 | with and convicted of the offence by virtue of this subsection whether
-- src:4868 | or not proceedings are taken against the firstmentioned person.
@ref s 53(5) (src:4864-4868)
GIVEN `the commission of the offence by another person was due to the act or default of this person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(5): this other person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    `the commission of the offence by another person was due to the act or default of this person`

-- src:4870 | (6) In any proceedings for an offence under this section, it is,
-- src:4871 | subject to subsection (7), a defence for the person charged to prove
-- src:4872 | that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due
-- src:4873 | diligence to avoid committing the offence.
@ref s 53(6) (src:4870-4873)
GIVEN `the person proves the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(6): the defence is made out` MEANS
    `the person proves the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence`

§ `s 54 Prohibitions in respect of telecommunication and radio-communication equipment`

-- The licence-or-regulations exception of s 54(1), read with s 56 (a licence recognised under a treaty) and with s 96
-- (an exemption by the Minister), which s 54 does not mention but s 56 and s 96 say apply to it.
-- src:4899 | (b) possess any radio-communication equipment,
-- src:4901 | except and in accordance with a licence granted under section 5 or
-- src:4902 | any regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 54(1) exception (src:4899-4902)
GIVEN held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` MEANS
        held's `a licence granted under section 5`
    OR held's `an authorisation given by regulations made under this Act`

-- src:4894 | 54.—(1) A person must not —
-- src:4896 | (a) offer for sale, sell or possess for sale any
-- src:4897 | telecommunication equipment; or
@ref s 54(1)(a) (src:4894-4897)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` MEANS
        `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it`
    AND `s 2: the equipment is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` e
    AND (NOT (`s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))

-- src:4899 | (b) possess any radio-communication equipment,
-- src:4901 | except and in accordance with a licence granted under section 5 or
-- src:4902 | any regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 54(1)(b) (src:4899-4902)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` MEANS
        `the person possesses it`
    AND `s 2 (composed): the equipment is radio-communication equipment` e
    AND (NOT (`s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))

-- src:4904 | (2) Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with
-- src:4905 | subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 54(2) (src:4904-4905)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
      `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Offence outcome`
`s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` MEANS
    IF     (   `s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` held
            OR `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` e `the person possesses it` held)
       AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
       AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))
       AND (NOT (`s 95: the Act does not apply to the licensing of this apparatus` `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` FALSE))
    THEN `an offence under` "section 54(2)" (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING)
    ELSE `no offence under this provision`

-- FORK 3, Reading B: s 95 does not displace the offence.
@ref s 54(2), s 95 Reading B (src:4904-4905)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A `Offence outcome`
`s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B of s 95` MEANS
    IF     (   `s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` held
            OR `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` e `the person possesses it` held)
       AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
       AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))
    THEN `an offence under` "section 54(2)" (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING)
    ELSE `no offence under this provision`

§ `s 55 Penalty for unlicensed station`

-- src:4911 | 55.—(1) Any person who establishes, installs, maintains, provides
-- src:4912 | or operates a radio‑communication system or service or any
-- src:4913 | radio‑communication equipment in any place or on board any
-- src:4914 | vessel, aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore without a licence
-- src:4915 | granted under section 5 or any regulations made under this Act shall
-- src:4916 | be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 55(1) (src:4911-4916)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      where IS A `Where the equipment is`
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service`
    AND `s 2 (composed): the equipment is radio-communication equipment` e
    AND (NOT (`s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))
    AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
    AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))

-- src:4918 | (2) Any person who is in possession of any radio‑communication
-- src:4919 | equipment is deemed, until the contrary is proved, to have operated
-- src:4920 | the same.
@ref s 55(2) (src:4918-4920)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of the radio-communication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55(2): the person is deemed to have operated it` MEANS
        `the person is in possession of the radio-communication equipment`
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- src:4922 | (3) The occupier of any dwelling house or premises in which is
-- src:4923 | installed any radio‑communication equipment in respect of which a
-- src:4924 | licence is not in force shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 55(3) (src:4922-4924)
GIVEN `the person is the occupier of a dwelling house or premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `radio-communication equipment is installed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a licence is in force in respect of that equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55(3): the occupier is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person is the occupier of a dwelling house or premises`
    AND `radio-communication equipment is installed in it`
    AND (NOT `a licence is in force in respect of that equipment`)

-- src:4926 | (4) It is a defence in any proceedings for an offence under
-- src:4927 | subsection (3) that the occupier was not aware and could not with
-- src:4928 | reasonable diligence have become aware of the existence in the
-- src:4929 | dwelling-house or premises of the radio‑communication equipment.
@ref s 55(4) (src:4926-4929)
GIVEN `the occupier was not aware` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupier could not with reasonable diligence have become aware of the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55(4): the defence is made out` MEANS
    `the occupier was not aware` AND `the occupier could not with reasonable diligence have become aware of the equipment`

§ `s 56 Exemption from sections 53, 54 and 55`

-- src:4935 | 56. Subject to such conditions as the Authority may impose,
-- src:4936 | sections 53, 54 and 55 do not apply to any person who has been issued
-- src:4938 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:4939 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 100
-- src:4941 | with a licence for the installation or working of any
-- src:4942 | telecommunication equipment under the provisions of any written
-- src:4943 | law in force in any country which is a party to a treaty or any other
-- src:4944 | arrangement to which Singapore is a party pursuant to which licences
-- src:4945 | issued under the written laws in force in each country for the
-- src:4946 | installation or working of any telecommunication equipment are
-- src:4947 | recognised as having force in the other country.
@ref s 56 (src:4935-4947)
GIVEN `the person has been issued a licence for the installation or working of telecommunication equipment under the written law of a country that is party to a treaty or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under that treaty or arrangement such licences are recognised as having force in each country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56: sections 53, 54 and 55 do not apply to the person (subject to the Authority's conditions)` MEANS
        `the person has been issued a licence for the installation or working of telecommunication equipment under the written law of a country that is party to a treaty or arrangement`
    AND `under that treaty or arrangement such licences are recognised as having force in each country`

§ `s 57 Powers of search and seizure`

-- src:4993 | (3) If there is no prosecution with regard to any equipment or
-- src:4994 | system seized under this section, the equipment or system is to be
-- src:4995 | taken and deemed to be forfeited to the Authority unless a claim is
-- src:4996 | made within 2 months after the date of seizure.
@ref s 57(3) (src:4993-4996)
GIVEN `there is no prosecution with regard to the equipment or system seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim is made within 2 months after the date of seizure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(3): the equipment or system is taken and deemed forfeited to the Authority` MEANS
    `there is no prosecution with regard to the equipment or system seized` AND (NOT `a claim is made within 2 months after the date of seizure`)

§ `s 58 Sealing of telecommunication system or equipment`

-- src:5024 | (2) Any person who, without lawful authority, breaks, tampers with
-- src:5025 | or damages any seal referred to in subsection (1), or removes any
-- src:5026 | telecommunication system or equipment or any
-- src:5027 | radio‑communication system or equipment which has been sealed
-- src:5029 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5030 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 102
-- src:5032 | under that subsection, or attempts to do so, shall be guilty of an
-- src:5033 | offence.
@ref s 58(2) (src:5024-5033)
GIVEN `the person broke, tampered with or damaged a seal, or removed sealed equipment, or attempted to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58(2): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person broke, tampered with or damaged a seal, or removed sealed equipment, or attempted to` AND (NOT `the person had lawful authority`)

§ `s 59 Using unlawful telecommunication system or service`

-- src:5039 | 59. Any person who knowing or having reason to believe that a
-- src:5040 | telecommunication system or service has been established, installed,
-- src:5041 | maintained, operated or provided in contravention of this Act,
-- src:5042 | whether or not such system or service is connected to or provided
-- src:5043 | through a public telecommunication licensee’s installation or plant,
-- src:5044 | uses the system or service for communication or for performing any
-- src:5045 | service incidental thereto or delivers any message for transmission by
-- src:5046 | the system or service or accepts delivery of any message sent shall be
-- src:5047 | guilty of an offence.
@ref s 59 (src:5039-5047)
GIVEN `the system or service was established, installed, maintained, operated or provided in contravention of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew or had reason to believe that` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person used it for communication or for performing any service incidental to it, or delivered or accepted a message for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the system or service was established, installed, maintained, operated or provided in contravention of the Act`
    AND `the person knew or had reason to believe that`
    AND `the person used it for communication or for performing any service incidental to it, or delivered or accepted a message for it`

§ `s 64 Possession or supply of any thing for fraudulent purpose`

-- src:5151 | 64.—(1) Subsection (2) applies if a person has in the custody or
-- src:5152 | under the control of the person any thing which may be used for the
-- src:5153 | purpose of obtaining, or for a purpose connected with the obtaining
-- src:5154 | of, a service to which section 63 applies.
-- src:5156 | (2) If the person intends —
-- src:5158 | (a) to use the thing mentioned in subsection (1) —
-- src:5160 | (i) to obtain such a service dishonestly; or
-- src:5162 | (ii) for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining
-- src:5163 | of such a service;
-- src:5165 | (b) dishonestly to allow the thing to be used to obtain such a
-- src:5166 | service; or
-- src:5168 | (c) to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with
-- src:5169 | the dishonest obtaining of such a service,
-- src:5171 | the person shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 64(1) and (2) (src:5151-5171)
GIVEN `the person has the thing in custody or under control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be used for obtaining, or for a purpose connected with obtaining, a service to which s 63 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to use it, or to allow it to be used, dishonestly to obtain such a service or for a purpose connected with that` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(2): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person has the thing in custody or under control`
    AND `it may be used for obtaining, or for a purpose connected with obtaining, a service to which s 63 applies`
    AND `the person intends to use it, or to allow it to be used, dishonestly to obtain such a service or for a purpose connected with that`

-- src:5202 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section shall be liable
-- src:5203 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment
-- src:5204 | for a term not exceeding 10 years or to both.
@ref s 64(5) (src:5202-5204)
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`s 64(5): the penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 100000, 120, 0, FALSE
